Summary of the most serious issues in 8/20:
- `ctlv_op_query_more()` (`frag_mark`) walks `ctx->deepest->up` through cursors that live on family stack frames. A normal "reply full" path abandons open nests without `ctlv_nest_end()`; the walk then dereferences dead stack and writes through a garbage ->start. Store open-nest offsets in the ctx instead.
- The ternary in `ctlv_op_error()`/`ctlv_op_errorf()` is dead; the result is always `-EINVAL`.
- A failed `nest_start()` leaves a zeroed child that makes a following `ctlv_nest_end()` WARN; the `MAX_NEST_DEPTH` check is documented as unreachable.
- Redundant `max_len` check in `ctlv_put_string()`, forward declaration of a static function, missing includes, detached non-kernel-doc comment block in `ctlv.h`.
